# 🏦 Bank Customer Churn Analysis

## 📌 Project Overview

This project analyzes customer churn in a banking dataset containing 10,000 customer records.

The goal is to identify customer characteristics and segments associated with higher churn and provide useful business insights for customer retention.

## 🛠️ Tools & Technologies

- Python
- Pandas
- NumPy
- Matplotlib
- Seaborn
- SQL
- Power BI

## 📊 Analysis Performed

### Customer Churn Analysis

- Overall Customer Churn Rate
- Customer Churn by Geography
- Customer Churn by Age Group
- Customer Churn by Gender
- Customer Churn by Credit Score
- Customer Churn by Number of Products
- Customer Churn by Account Balance
- Customer Churn by Tenure
- Customer Churn by Active Membership

### SQL Analysis

SQL queries were used to analyze:

- Churn by Geography
- Churn by Number of Products
- Churn by Balance Group
- Churn by Active Membership
- Churn by Gender and Age Group

## 📈 Power BI Dashboard

A Power BI dashboard was created to visualize important customer churn patterns and provide an interactive view of the analysis.

## 🔍 Key Findings

- The overall customer churn rate is **25%**.
- France has the highest churn rate among the three geographies.
- Customers with higher account balances show substantially higher churn in this dataset.
- Customers with 3 or 4 products have higher churn rates than customers with fewer products.
- Churn rates are relatively similar across male and female customers.

## 💡 Business Recommendations

- Identify and proactively engage high-balance customers at risk of leaving.
- Investigate customers holding multiple products for possible dissatisfaction or service issues.
- Develop targeted retention campaigns for high-risk customer segments.
- Use customer characteristics and behavioral patterns to improve retention strategies.

